  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon there is an upper-level ridge over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will keep warm and mostly\ndry weather for the area on Monday. Isolated showers have the \npotential to slide south from Canada and affect the Hi-Line this \nafternoon and evening. On Tuesday the upper-level ridge remains \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Monday. This will \nwill keep warm and mostly dry weather for the area on Tuesday. \nIsolated showers have the potential to slide south from Canada and\naffect the Hi-Line Tuesday afternoon and evening. On Wednesday \nthe upper-level ridge remains over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana with an upper-level trough approaching the \narea. This will begin to bring cooler air and monsoonal moisture \nto the area on Wednesday. On Wednesday there will be showers and \nthunderstorms along the Hi-Line. \n\nThursday through Friday an upper-level trough moves over North- \ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring \nshowers and thunderstorms and cooler temperatures (well-below \nseasonal averages) to the area Thursday through Friday. See the \nForecast Confidence & Scenarios section for details. This weekend \nan upper-level ridge builds back in over North-central, Central, \nand Southwestern Montana with southwest flow aloft. This will \nbring daily chances for showers and thunderstorms with \ntemperatures warming up on Saturday and Sunday. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nThis afternoon and tomorrow afternoon across North-central, Central, \nand Southwestern Montana minimum afternoon humidity will be near \ncritical levels. This combined with winds that will be around 20 \nmph will bring elevated fire weather conditions to the area. The \nwind direction will also periodically shift over the next 24 \nhours. The greatest risk for elevated to near critical fire \nweather conditions will be in Southwestern Montana this afternoon \nand tomorrow afternoon. \n\nWednesday through Friday there is good agreement between ensemble \nmembers and deterministic models in the track of the upper-level \ntrough. On Wednesday there is a 20 - 35% chance for thunderstorms \nacross North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On \nThursday there is a 30 - 50% chance for thunderstorms across \nNorth-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On Friday there\nis a 35 - 55% chance for thunderstorms across Central and \nSouthwestern Montana. Wednesday through Friday there is a 50 - \n80% chance for one half inch of rain or greater across North- \ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana with the highest \nprobabilities along the Hi-Line. Wednesday through Friday there is\na 50 - 70% chance for one inch of rain or greater along the Hi- \nLine and across Judith Basin and Fergus Counties. On Thursday and \nFriday there is greater than a 60% chance for high temperatures of\n70 degrees or lower across the plains of North-central Montana. \n-IG",
